Because the difficulties, perceived by some, in reading top-posted or
otherwise pooh-poohed posts, don't match reality most of the time.
Because people, in informal, recreational forums such as r.g.r.n and
most Usenet groups, should be able to express themselves without
having to worry about rigid syntactic rules enforced by guard dog
mentalities.  Because communication is dictated by the transmitter,
not just on Usenet but in most daily situations, and successful
communication always involves the ability to read or listen well.  All
communicators "force" others to read them in a specific way.  That's
not a crime.

